, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn6le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn6le02ob01re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn6le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn6le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Lady Diana Spencer was born in 1961. She had a normal, quiet upbringing. </p>It did not prepare her for the fame and glamour of being a British princess. Within a few years, she changed from being a shy teenager to the most photographed person on the planet.\nDiana was a kindergarten teacher in London when she caught the interest of Prince Charles. She won the hearts of a nation with her shy smiles and natural beauty. The whole world watched the fairytale royal wedding in 1981."}, {"time": "35000", "image": "engenn6le02ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Diana was nervous at first in public, but she quickly developed a charming manner. She immediately took a strong interest in many charities and important causes. She highlighted the suffering of the homeless, lepers and AIDS victims. She also strongly campaigned for the abolition of landmines and many countries banned them."}, {"time": "57000", "image": "engenn6le02ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "She constantly made newspaper headlines around the world, but the biggest one was for her death at the age of 36. At her funeral, British Prime Minister Tony Blair called her the \u201cPeople's Princess\". To many, she was simply the \u201cQueen of Hearts\"."}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}]}]}